/*
# MonthCalendar

A month of days to pick one from: the month and year with buttons to the months either
side, a row of weekday initials, and six weeks of days. Days of the months either side
fill the first and last weeks, in muted ink, and pressing one picks it and shows its
month. Today wears a ring; the chosen day is filled.

Its value is a date as an ISO string, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`, or `""` for none — the value
pattern, as every control has it: standalone it keeps its own, constrained it delivers
through `input`.

```declare
App [ width = 300, height = 340, day: string = "2026-10-18",
    MonthCalendar [ x = 20, y = 20, value = { app.day }, min = "2026-10-05",
        input(v: string) { app.day = v } ],
    Text [ x = 20, y = 310, text = { app.day } ]
    ]
```

The days are one Tab stop, as a screen reader's grid: Tab lands on the chosen day, else
today, else the 1st. The arrows move a day left and right and a week up and down, into
the next or previous month when they cross its edge; Page Up and Page Down move a month
(with Shift, a year); Home and End go to the start and end of the week; Enter or Space
picks. The month buttons are Tab stops of their own, before the days.

Names come from the program's language (`app.language`): the month, the weekday
initials, and each day's full date, which is what a screen reader says on it.

## value
The chosen day, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`, or `""` for none. Constrain it to your own state and
override `input` beside it, or leave it and read it back.

## input()
**Where a pick goes**, receiving the day. The default writes `value`.

## min
The first day that can be picked, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`; days before it are disabled. `""`
for no limit.

## max
The last day that can be picked; days after it are disabled. `""` for no limit.

## weekStart
The day a week starts on: `0` Sunday (the default), `1` Monday, and so on.

## daySize
The width and height of a day, 32 by default.

## today
Today, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`, from the calendar's own clock, so it turns over at midnight.

## shownMonth
The month on screen, `"YYYY-MM"`: the value's month, else today's, until the month
buttons, the keys or a pick move it. Set it to show another month.

## title
The shown month and year as the language writes them, "October 2026" — the header's
text and the name of the grid.

## gridW
The width of seven days, which the header and the weekday row share.

## pad2()
A number as two digits.

## isoOf()
The ISO date of a year, a month (1–12) and a day.

## dateOf()
The local date an ISO date names, at midnight — never parsed as UTC, so it is the same
day in every time zone.

## isoOfDate()
The ISO date of a local date.

## addDays()
The ISO date *n* days on (or back, when *n* is negative).

## addMonths()
The ISO date *n* months on, kept inside the month it lands in: a month on from
January 31 is the last day of February.

## clamp()
A day moved inside `min` and `max`.

## weeks()
The six weeks on screen, as records — each day's `iso`, its `day` of the month, whether
it is `inMonth`, `today`, `selected` or `disabled`, and its full `name` — the data the
grid replicates.

## weekdayNames()
The seven weekday initials, from `weekStart`.

## step()
Shows the month *n* months on.

## pick()
Picks a day: shows its month and delivers it through `input`.

## entryDay()
The day Tab lands on in the shown month: the chosen day, else today, else the 1st —
kept inside `min` and `max`.

## cellFor()
The day view showing a date, or null when it is not on screen.

## go()
Answers a key on a day: works out the day it moves to, shows that day's month, and
moves the focus to it once the month is on screen. False for a key it does not move by.

## moveTo()
Shows a day's month and moves the focus to the day.

## width
The width of seven days.
*/

/*
# MonthCalendarDay

One day of a `MonthCalendar`, **made from the calendar's week records — never written
directly**. A `Control`, so the focus moves from day to day and a screen reader says
each one, by its full date. Pressing it, or Enter or Space on it, picks it.

```declare
App [ width = 200, height = 64,
    day: Dataset { { "iso": "2026-10-18", "day": 18, "inMonth": true, "selected": true,
                     "name": "Sunday, October 18, 2026" } },
    MonthCalendarDay [ x = 20, y = 16, datapath = { app.day.value } ]
    ]
```

## iso
The date it shows, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`.

## picked()
What a pick does — the calendar that places a day says.

## navigate()
What a key does on it before the control's own keys — the calendar that places a day
moves the focus with it. True when the key was used.

## press()
Picks the day.

## onKeyDown
The calendar's keys first; then Enter and Space pick.

## ink
The day's number colour: on the accent when chosen, muted outside the shown month.

## accessibilityRole
`cell`, one of the grid's.

## accessibilityLabel
The full date, "Sunday, October 18, 2026", as the language writes it.

## accessibilitySelected
Whether it is the chosen day.

## disabled
Outside `min` and `max`: not focusable, not pickable, dimmed.

## width
32 — the calendar sets its `daySize`.

## height
As wide as it is tall.

## cornerRadius
Round.

## fill
The accent when chosen; the theme's hover and pressed fills otherwise; nothing at rest.

## stroke
A ring in the accent on today.

## opacity
Dimmed to the theme's `disabledOpacity` when disabled.

## accentFill
The chosen day's ground: the theme's accent, or its hovered or pressed shade.

## plainFill
Any other day's ground: the control's hovered or pressed shade, or none at rest.
*/

/*
# MonthCalendarArrow

A month button of a `MonthCalendar`: a quiet control with a chevron, no fill until the
pointer is over it. The calendar that places it says what pressing it does.

```declare
App [ width = 200, height = 64, n: number = 0,
    MonthCalendarArrow [ x = 20, y = 18, dir = -1, press() { app.n = app.n - 1 } ],
    MonthCalendarArrow [ x = 52, y = 18, press() { app.n = app.n + 1 } ],
    Text [ x = 100, y = 22, text = { "" + app.n } ]
    ]
```

## dir
Which way it points: `-1` back, `1` on.

## accessibilityRole
A button.

## accessibilityLabel
"Previous month" or "Next month".

## width
28.

## height
28.

## cornerRadius
The theme's `controlCornerRadius`.

## fill
The theme's hover and pressed fills; nothing at rest.

## opacity
Dimmed to the theme's `disabledOpacity` when disabled.
*/

/*
# DatePicker

A field that shows a date and opens a month to pick one from. Press it — or Enter,
Space or Down on it — and a `Popover` opens below it holding a `MonthCalendar`, with the
focus on the chosen day; picking a day sets it and closes, and the focus goes back to
the field. Esc, or a press past it, closes without picking.

```declare
App [ width = 340, height = 380, due: string = "",
    DatePicker [ x = 20, y = 20, value = { app.due },
        input(v: string) { app.due = v } ],
    Text [ x = 20, y = 70, text = { app.due == "" ? "no date" : "due " + app.due } ]
    ]
```

It looks like a `Combobox`'s field: the theme's field fill and line, its height and
corners, a chevron at the end. The date shows in the program's language
(`app.language`) at medium length, "Oct 18, 2026".

## value
The chosen day, `"YYYY-MM-DD"`, or `""` for none. Constrain it to your own state and
override `input` beside it, or leave it and read it back.

## input()
**Where a pick goes**, receiving the day. The default writes `value`.

## min
The first day that can be picked; `""` for no limit.

## max
The last day that can be picked; `""` for no limit.

## weekStart
The day the calendar's weeks start on: `0` Sunday, `1` Monday.

## placeholder
What the field shows with no date, "Select a date" by default.

## display
The date as the field shows it, or `""` with none.

## formatted()
A date as the language writes it at medium length, "Oct 18, 2026"; `""` for none.

## open()
Opens the calendar on the chosen day's month (else today's), unless it is open.

## choose()
Closes the calendar and delivers the day through `input`.

## press()
Opens the calendar, or closes it if it is open.

## onKeyDown
Down opens the calendar too; Enter and Space press.

## accessibilityRole
A button: pressing it opens the calendar.

## accessibilityExpanded
Whether the calendar is open.

## accessibilityLabel
The caption of a `Field` around it, with the date after it; with no caption, the field's
own text names it.

## width
180.

## height
The theme's `comboboxHeight`.

## fill
The theme's `surface`, as a field.

## stroke
The theme's `line`, and the `accent` while the calendar is open.

## cornerRadius
The theme's `fieldCornerRadius`, else `controlCornerRadius`.

## opacity
Dimmed to the theme's `disabledOpacity` when disabled.
*/

include [ "control.declare", "popover.declare", "spacer.declare", "textlabel.declare", "icons/core.declare" ]

class MonthCalendar [
    value: string = "",
    min: string = "",
    max: string = "",
    weekStart: number = 0,
    daySize: number = 32,

    input(v: string) { value = v },

    clock: Time [ tick = day ],
    today: string = { this.isoOf(this.clock.year, this.clock.month, this.clock.day) },
    shownMonth: string = { (value != "" ? value : today).slice(0, 7) },
    title: string = { this.dateOf(shownMonth).toLocaleDateString(app.language, ({ month: "long", year: "numeric" })) },
    gridW: number = { 7 * daySize + 12 },
    width = { this.gridW },

    // ── dates: local days built from year, month and day, never parsed as UTC ──

    pad2(n: number) -> string { return (n < 10 ? "0" : "") + n },
    isoOf(y: number, m: number, d: number) -> string { return y + "-" + this.pad2(m) + "-" + this.pad2(d) },
    dateOf(iso: string) -> Date {
        const p = iso.split("-").map((s) => parseInt(s, 10))
        return new Date(p[0], (p[1] ?? 1) - 1, p[2] ?? 1)
        },
    isoOfDate(d: Date) -> string { return this.isoOf(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth() + 1, d.getDate()) },
    addDays(iso: string, n: number) -> string {
        const d = this.dateOf(iso)
        return this.isoOfDate(new Date(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth(), d.getDate() + n))
        },
    addMonths(iso: string, n: number) -> string {
        const d = this.dateOf(iso)
        const last = new Date(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth() + n + 1, 0).getDate()
        return this.isoOfDate(new Date(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth() + n, Math.min(d.getDate(), last)))
        },
    clamp(iso: string) -> string {
        if (min != "" && iso < min) return min
        if (max != "" && iso > max) return max
        return iso
        },

    // ── the six weeks on screen, as data ──────────────────────────────────

    weeks() -> array {
        const first = this.dateOf(shownMonth + "-01")
        const lead = (first.getDay() - weekStart + 7) % 7
        const named = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(app.language, ({ weekday: "long", year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" }))
        const out = []
        for (let w = 0; w < 6; w++) {
            const days = []
            for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++) {
                const d = new Date(first.getFullYear(), first.getMonth(), 1 - lead + w * 7 + i)
                const iso = this.isoOfDate(d)
                days.push(({ id: "d" + i, iso: iso, day: d.getDate(),
                    inMonth: d.getMonth() == first.getMonth(), today: iso == today, selected: iso == value,
                    disabled: (min != "" && iso < min) || (max != "" && iso > max), name: named.format(d) }))
                }
            out.push(({ id: "w" + w, days: days }))
            }
        return out
        },

    weekdayNames() -> array {
        const f = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(app.language, ({ weekday: "narrow" }))
        return [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((i) => ({ id: "k" + i, label: f.format(new Date(2023, 0, 1 + (weekStart + i) % 7)) }))
        },

    model: Dataset [ contents = { { weeks: classroot.weeks() } } ],
    initials: Dataset [ contents = { { days: classroot.weekdayNames() } } ],

    // ── what the buttons and keys do ──────────────────────────────────────

    step(n: number) { shownMonth = this.addMonths(shownMonth + "-01", n).slice(0, 7) },

    pick(iso: string) {
        const moved = iso.slice(0, 7) != shownMonth
        shownMonth = iso.slice(0, 7)
        if (moved && Focus.holds(this.grid)) afterSettle(() => { const c = this.cellFor(iso); if (c != null) Focus.focus(c) })
        input(iso)
        },

    entryDay() -> string {
        const d = value.startsWith(shownMonth) ? value : today.startsWith(shownMonth) ? today : shownMonth + "-01"
        return this.clamp(d)
        },

    cellFor(iso: string) -> View? {
        for (const r of this.grid.children) {
            for (const c of (r as View).children ?? []) if ((c as MonthCalendarDay).iso === iso) return c as View
            }
        return null
        },

    go(from: string, e: KeyEvent) -> boolean {
        const d = this.dateOf(from)
        const back = (d.getDay() - weekStart + 7) % 7
        let to = ""
        if (e.key == "ArrowLeft") to = this.addDays(from, -1)
        else if (e.key == "ArrowRight") to = this.addDays(from, 1)
        else if (e.key == "ArrowUp") to = this.addDays(from, -7)
        else if (e.key == "ArrowDown") to = this.addDays(from, 7)
        else if (e.key == "Home") to = this.addDays(from, -back)
        else if (e.key == "End") to = this.addDays(from, 6 - back)
        else if (e.key == "PageUp") to = this.addMonths(from, e.shift ? -12 : -1)
        else if (e.key == "PageDown") to = this.addMonths(from, e.shift ? 12 : 1)
        else return false
        this.moveTo(this.clamp(to))
        return true
        },

    moveTo(iso: string) {
        shownMonth = iso.slice(0, 7)
        afterSettle(() => { const c = this.cellFor(iso); if (c != null) Focus.focus(c) })
        },

    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 6 ],

    // the month and year, and the buttons to the months either side

    header: View [ width = { classroot.gridW }, height = 30,
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = 2 ],
        heading: View [ y = center, padding = [0, 0, 0, 6], accessibilityRole = heading, accessibilityLive = polite,
            Text [ fontSize = 14, fontWeight = semibold, wrap = false, textColor = { provided("theme").text }, text = { classroot.title } ]
            ],
        Spacer [ ],
        prev: MonthCalendarArrow [ dir = -1, y = center,
            disabled = { classroot.min != "" && classroot.shownMonth <= classroot.min.slice(0, 7) },
            press() { if (!disabled) classroot.step(-1) }
            ],
        next: MonthCalendarArrow [ dir = 1, y = center,
            disabled = { classroot.max != "" && classroot.shownMonth >= classroot.max.slice(0, 7) },
            press() { if (!disabled) classroot.step(1) }
            ]
        ],

    // the weekday initials are read in each day's name, so to a screen reader
    // the row is decoration: a picture with no name

    weekdays: View [ height = 20, accessibilityRole = image, datapath = { classroot.initials.value },
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = 2 ],
        View [ datapath = :days[], width = { classroot.daySize }, height = 20,
            TextLabel [ x = center, fontSize = 11, fontWeight = medium, wrap = false,
                textColor = { provided("theme").textMuted }, text = { "" + :label } ]
            ]
        ],

    // one Tab stop, landing on the chosen day; the days take their own keys

    grid: View [ accessibilityRole = grid, accessibilityLabel = { classroot.title }, focusScope = stop,
        focusEntry() -> View? { return classroot.cellFor(classroot.entryDay()) },
        datapath = { classroot.model.value },
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 2 ],
        View [ datapath = :weeks[], accessibilityRole = row,
            layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = 2 ],
            MonthCalendarDay [ datapath = :days[], width = { classroot.daySize },
                picked() { classroot.pick(this.iso) },
                navigate(e: KeyEvent) -> boolean { return classroot.go(this.iso, e) }
                ]
            ]
        ]
    ]


class MonthCalendarDay extends Control [
    accessibilityRole = cell,
    accessibilityLabel = { "" + (:name ?? "") },
    accessibilitySelected = { :selected == true },
    disabled = { :disabled == true },

    iso: string = { "" + (:iso ?? "") },

    width = 32,
    height = { this.width },
    cornerRadius = { this.width / 2 },
    accentFill: Color = { pressed ? provided("theme").accentPressed : hovered ? provided("theme").accentHovered : provided("theme").accent },
    plainFill: Color? = { pressed ? provided("theme").controlPressed : hovered ? provided("theme").controlHovered : null },
    fill = { :selected == true ? this.accentFill : this.plainFill },
    stroke = { :today == true && :selected != true ? stroke(1.5, provided("theme").accent) : null },
    opacity = { disabled ? (provided("theme").disabledOpacity) : 1 },

    ink: Color = { :selected == true ? provided("theme").accentTextColor
        : :inMonth == true ? provided("theme").text : provided("theme").textMuted },

    // the number is what the eye reads; a screen reader hears the full date,
    // so to it the number is decoration — a picture with no name

    num: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, accessibilityRole = image,
        t: TextLabel [ x = center, fontSize = 13, wrap = false,
            fontWeight = { :selected == true || :today == true ? "semibold" : "regular" },
            textColor = { classroot.ink }, text = { "" + (:day ?? "") } ]
        ],

    picked() { },
    navigate(e: KeyEvent) -> boolean { return false },
    press() { if (!disabled) picked() },
    onKeyDown(e: KeyEvent) {
        if (navigate(e)) return
        super.onKeyDown(e)
        }
    ]


class MonthCalendarArrow extends Control [
    dir: number = 1,
    accessibilityRole = button,
    accessibilityLabel = { dir < 0 ? "Previous month" : "Next month" },
    width = 28,
    height = 28,
    cornerRadius = { provided("theme").controlCornerRadius },
    fill = { pressed ? provided("theme").controlPressed : hovered ? provided("theme").controlHovered : null },
    opacity = { disabled ? (provided("theme").disabledOpacity) : 1 },
    g: ChevronIcon [ iconSize = 14, x = center, y = center,
        dir = { classroot.dir < 0 ? "left" : "right" },
        ink = { classroot.hovered || classroot.pressed ? provided("theme").text : provided("theme").textMuted } ]
    ]


class DatePicker extends Control [
    accessibilityRole = button,
    accessibilityExpanded = { this.pop.shown },
    accessibilityLabel = { provided("fieldLabel", "") != "" ? provided("fieldLabel", "") + (display != "" ? ", " + display : "") : "" },

    value: string = "",
    min: string = "",
    max: string = "",
    weekStart: number = 0,
    placeholder: string = "Select a date",

    input(v: string) { value = v },

    display: string = { this.formatted(value, app.language) },

    width = 180,
    height = { provided("theme").comboboxHeight },
    fill = { provided("theme").surface },
    stroke = { stroke(1, this.pop.shown ? provided("theme").accent : provided("theme").line) },
    cornerRadius = { provided("theme").fieldCornerRadius ?? provided("theme").controlCornerRadius },
    opacity = { disabled ? (provided("theme").disabledOpacity) : 1 },

    formatted(iso: string, lang: string) -> string {
        if (iso == "") return ""
        const p = iso.split("-").map((s) => parseInt(s, 10))
        const d = new Date(p[0], (p[1] ?? 1) - 1, p[2] ?? 1)
        return isNaN(d.getTime()) ? iso : d.toLocaleDateString(lang, ({ dateStyle: "medium" }))
        },

    open() {
        if (this.pop.shown || disabled) return
        const c = this.pop.cal
        if (c != null) c.shownMonth = (value != "" ? value : c.today).slice(0, 7)
        this.pop.showFor(this)
        },

    choose(v: string) {
        this.pop.close()
        input(v)
        },

    // a press on the field while the calendar is open closes it as a press
    // past it; the click that follows must not open it again

    press() {
        if (this.pop.shown) this.pop.close()
        else if (!this.pop.present) this.open()
        },

    onKeyDown(e: KeyEvent) {
        if (!disabled && !e.repeat && e.key == "ArrowDown") { this.open(); return }
        super.onKeyDown(e)
        },

    label: TextLabel [ x = { provided("theme").fieldPadding ?? 10 }, wrap = false,
        width = { classroot.width - this.x - 26 }, clip = true,
        textColor = { classroot.display == "" ? provided("theme").textMuted : provided("theme").text },
        text = { classroot.display == "" ? classroot.placeholder : classroot.display } ],

    mark: ChevronIcon [ iconSize = 13, ink = { provided("theme").textMuted }, y = center,
        x = { classroot.width - 13 - 6 - 4 } ],

    pop: Popover [ accessibilityLabel = { provided("fieldLabel", "") || classroot.placeholder },
        focusFirst() {
            const c = this.cal
            const v = c.cellFor(c.entryDay())
            if (v != null) Focus.focus(v)
            else Focus.focusIn(this)
            },
        cal: MonthCalendar [ value = { classroot.value }, min = { classroot.min }, max = { classroot.max },
            weekStart = { classroot.weekStart },
            input(v: string) { classroot.choose(v) }
            ]
        ]
    ]
